    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1169">

                <pb facs="1706" n="1690" sameAs="frus:frus1949v06/pg1690"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">745.45F/1–2449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in India</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Henderson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New Delhi</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-01-24T14:00:00+05:30">January 24, 1949—2
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>119. Deptel 35, January 14.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1169-f1"/> We believe arms embargo should now be dropped as soon as
                    possible and in same quiet way it was imposed. In our view this action need not
                    be linked with any specific development such as appointment of PA or signing of truce agreement. On contrary we
                    would hope that Department would advise GOI and
                        GOP representatives that action is being
                    taken because we have confidence <pb facs="1707" n="1691" xml:id="pg1691"/> In
                    good faith and desire of both parties to reach peaceful settlement Kashmir
                    dispute. At same time it might be made clear that if for any reason fighting
                    should again break out embargo would probably be reinstituted. We assume also
                    Department would give both parties to understand that US does not have large
                    quantities arms available.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 119, pouched Karachi.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henderson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
